WEBVTT

02:39.326 --> 02:40.805
What happened to your face?

02:41.161 --> 02:44.973
Pool game the other night,
called the wrong dude on cheating.

02:47.100 --> 02:48.443
You gotta watch that.

02:51.438 --> 02:52.781
What do you want, again?

02:54.541 --> 02:56.316
I'm repping some people.

02:56.376 --> 02:58.879
And they want to get to the good cook.

02:58.979 --> 03:02.483
They'll trade you or the IC Brotherhood,
however you want to do it.

03:02.783 --> 03:04.126
Coke for crystal.

03:07.320 --> 03:08.993
Why ain't I talking to Miles?

03:09.056 --> 03:13.505
Me and Ginger go way back,
boosted together.

03:15.562 --> 03:16.836
You ain't saying much.

03:16.897 --> 03:19.138
I figure I'd let my man
give you the details.

03:19.199 --> 03:20.974
Look, this shit I got,

03:21.802 --> 03:24.646
you step on it five, six
times, it'll still kick.

03:24.705 --> 03:28.653
This means you got to cook a little more,
for a lot more profit.

03:32.312 --> 03:33.313
Nah.

03:34.147 --> 03:37.321
I ain't got no use for it. Or your money.

03:38.151 --> 03:40.153
My money don't spend?

03:42.155 --> 03:45.432
I can see your soul at
the edges of your eyes.

03:46.059 --> 03:48.539
It's corrosive, like acid.

03:50.564 --> 03:52.601
You got a demon, little man.

03:53.533 --> 03:55.069
And I don't like your face.

03:55.402 --> 03:57.712
It makes me want to do things to it.

03:59.239 --> 04:00.240
Ginger'?

04:00.941 --> 04:03.751
You call me again, I'm
setting Miles on you.

04:06.079 --> 04:07.786
I see you again,

04:08.548 --> 04:10.027
I'm putting you down.

04:11.351 --> 04:13.729
There's a shadow on you, son.

04:39.412 --> 04:40.618
Marty?

04:40.714 --> 04:43.888
You got him? You fucking better,
the shit I've been through.

04:43.950 --> 04:46.089
I do. I got him.

04:46.453 --> 04:49.593
We're on empty roads now, so I got
to drop back or he'll spot the tail.

04:49.990 --> 04:53.995
That's Reggie Ledoux's cook partner,
Dewall. Bird-dog him, Marty.

04:54.094 --> 04:55.266
Got it.

04:55.328 --> 04:57.137
Whats your location?

04:57.230 --> 05:00.074
Just south of I-10
along the Creole Nature Trail.

05:00.133 --> 05:02.977
Heading toward Carlyss. Hurry up, man.

05:03.069 --> 05:04.844
Copy that. On my way.

05:19.820 --> 05:21.663
How we doing back there, Ginger'?

05:22.756 --> 05:24.463
Fuck you, motherfucker!

05:26.593 --> 05:27.765
Yeah.

05:31.598 --> 05:33.339
How did you get onto Ledoux?

05:33.433 --> 05:37.939
One of my old Cl's tipped me off
the location of his cookhouse.

05:39.506 --> 05:41.952
So I came back on the job.

05:43.944 --> 05:46.948
Didn't want anybody else to catch him,
bring him in.

05:49.449 --> 05:50.792
Look, you want my help?

05:51.451 --> 05:53.522
Just show me the rest of the file.

05:53.620 --> 05:56.362
Why are you so hot to see
the new discovery file, man?

05:58.892 --> 06:00.200
Why are y'all

06:01.061 --> 06:03.905
so hot to not give it to me?

06:05.298 --> 06:08.006
It's supposed to be like
a consultation, right?

06:09.069 --> 06:11.572
Yeah, but, uh, you go first.

06:12.472 --> 06:16.010
You take me through it
and I'll let you see what we got.

06:20.380 --> 06:21.825
I'll hold you to that.

06:49.009 --> 06:50.249
When-is Ginger'?

06:50.377 --> 06:52.220
Wrapped up in a ditch.

06:52.445 --> 06:53.753
What you got?

06:53.847 --> 06:54.917
Lost him a minute.

06:55.015 --> 06:58.087
I had to double back a few times
till I found the exit.

06:58.184 --> 06:59.720
That's his truck there.

07:00.754 --> 07:03.030
We're gonna have to call this in, Rust.

07:03.623 --> 07:05.603
Eh, we don't want to do that.

07:06.192 --> 07:09.036
Troops will come ﬂood these woods.
They could scatter.

07:12.432 --> 07:14.878
All right, we ain't gonna
find him from here.

07:21.074 --> 07:23.111
You ever been hunting, Marty?

07:23.576 --> 07:25.954
Uh, yeah.

07:26.046 --> 07:29.721
Ten-point buck, year before last, 50 yards.

07:32.319 --> 07:34.120
I'm not talking about
sitting in a tree house

07:34.154 --> 07:37.067
waiting to ambush a buck
come to sniff your gash bait.

07:37.557 --> 07:39.002
Talking about tracking.

07:39.092 --> 07:40.935
Jesus' you're a prick.

07:40.994 --> 07:43.907
Look, we find the place,
we come back here, we call it in.

07:43.964 --> 07:45.966
One of us stays surveillance, yeah?

07:47.300 --> 07:48.904
I can live with that.

07:50.570 --> 07:51.810
Let's go.

07:51.905 --> 07:54.283
So you got a tip
where Ledoux cooks,

07:54.341 --> 07:57.151
and Cohle came back from wherever he was.

07:57.777 --> 08:00.587
You knew it was gonna get here, man.
Just the once.

08:01.247 --> 08:02.954
The way you tell it.

08:04.584 --> 08:07.121
I tell it the same way
that I told the shooting board

08:07.187 --> 08:10.862
and every cop bar
between Houston and Biloxi.

08:10.957 --> 08:14.871
And you know why
the story's always the same, 17 years gone?

08:15.462 --> 08:18.102
Because it only went down the one way.

08:19.766 --> 08:22.872
Now, Rust's dad taught him bow-hunting.

08:22.969 --> 08:28.942
You know, he had to track game
iii! he got within maybe 30 yards of it.

08:38.885 --> 08:42.856
Now, this enabled us
to discern the suspect's path

08:42.956 --> 08:48.304
while sidestepping the various
anti-intruder devices they installed.

10:04.938 --> 10:08.317
Trip wires back there.
The clearings probably mined.

10:09.109 --> 10:10.110
All right.

10:10.743 --> 10:12.552
How do you want to do it?

10:13.480 --> 10:16.393
You go back, call it in. I'll wait here.

10:18.718 --> 10:21.164
- You're gonna hold position?
- Yeah.

10:27.160 --> 10:28.935
Do it now, Marty.

10:29.796 --> 10:32.902
Fuck you. You ain't doing this without me.

10:47.580 --> 10:49.025
All right, stay low.

10:54.921 --> 10:56.696
We were just about to turn back,

10:56.923 --> 10:59.199
call in Parish, State, whoever.

11:00.260 --> 11:01.637
I mean, we had the location,

11:01.694 --> 11:05.267
we had our suspects identified
at the location, you know.

11:05.431 --> 11:08.708
Might as well just leave the shit be
and hand it off.

11:09.035 --> 11:11.606
But that ain't what happened. Hmm.

11:13.540 --> 11:16.714
No, as soon as we started
to back off, man...

11:16.809 --> 11:17.810
Blam!

11:18.378 --> 11:20.517
Bullets cut through right near Rust's head.

11:20.613 --> 11:24.390
We dove opposite ways into the high growth.

11:24.517 --> 11:28.397
But they'd already spotted us,
and they had something high-velocity...

11:28.488 --> 11:29.489
Boom!

11:29.789 --> 11:32.633
Blew apart this tree between us.

11:32.792 --> 11:34.032
I mean, it was on.

11:38.031 --> 11:39.032
Hmm.

11:39.499 --> 11:40.569
Heavy shit.

11:40.667 --> 11:44.877
Fucking ferns and whatnot bursting all
around us, bark flying off of trees.

11:44.971 --> 11:46.532
I mean, we were in a fucking shitstorm.

12:10.763 --> 12:11.764
Shh!

13:08.721 --> 13:11.600
State Police! Put your hands on your head.

13:12.458 --> 13:14.597
Put 'em on your head, now.

13:14.661 --> 13:16.834
Don't even think about it.

13:17.297 --> 13:19.004
Put your hands on your head right now.

13:19.732 --> 13:21.177
Intertwine your fingers.

13:22.135 --> 13:24.741
Do it! Back up toward me.

13:30.410 --> 13:32.447
Down on your knees. Come on.

13:38.418 --> 13:40.159
It's time, isn't it?

13:41.688 --> 13:43.292
The black star.

13:43.356 --> 13:44.801
Shut the fuck up.

13:58.471 --> 14:01.384
They'd spotted us
before we crossed the forest,

14:01.474 --> 14:05.149
so all we could do was
duck for cover, dig in,

14:05.812 --> 14:07.052
try getting closer.

14:07.146 --> 14:08.147
Um...

14:09.015 --> 14:10.392
It was chaos.

14:30.036 --> 14:31.379
The black stars rise.

14:33.072 --> 14:34.210
Why the antlers?

14:40.046 --> 14:42.720
Freeze, motherfucker. Put it down.
Hands up.

14:42.815 --> 14:44.317
State Police.

14:54.494 --> 14:55.598
Set it down.

14:55.995 --> 14:57.770
I know what happens next.

14:58.698 --> 15:00.678
I saw you in my dream.

15:01.000 --> 15:02.843
You're in Carcosa now

15:03.336 --> 15:04.337
with me.

15:05.505 --> 15:06.916
He sees you.

15:09.675 --> 15:10.676
Marty!

15:21.587 --> 15:23.396
You'll do this again.

15:24.090 --> 15:25.967
Time is a ﬂat circle.

15:26.058 --> 15:29.198
What's that, Nietzsche?
Shut the fuck up. Put it down!

15:29.262 --> 15:31.242
HART; Marty!

15:32.465 --> 15:33.569
There you go.

15:33.800 --> 15:35.746
Black stars.

15:36.636 --> 15:39.913
- They're coming from the sky.
- Put your hands on your head.

16:08.434 --> 16:12.143
While I was hunkered down
behind this old decrepit boat,

16:12.338 --> 16:16.309
Captain America, Marty Hart,
decides he's gonna run deep into the woods,

16:16.409 --> 16:19.754
flank around the back of the house,
where Ledoux's firing at us, right?

16:20.079 --> 16:21.990
Well, he sneaks up behind Ledoux,

16:22.081 --> 16:24.357
and just as Ledoux turns... Bam!

16:25.084 --> 16:26.427
Popped one off in him.

16:26.486 --> 16:28.488
Head shot' clean, dropped him.

16:29.155 --> 16:32.102
His buddy, Dewall, he made a run for it.

16:32.859 --> 16:37.604
And his homemade cracker-ass
security system took care of the rest.

16:42.034 --> 16:43.035
Oh, fuck.

16:45.605 --> 16:49.348
Get the cuffs off him before his blood
settles. We gotta make this look right.

16:57.950 --> 16:59.827
Goddamn. Fuck.

17:24.477 --> 17:25.922
What do we do, Rust?

17:26.012 --> 17:27.150
Fuck him.

17:27.713 --> 17:29.715
Good to see you commit to something.

17:29.815 --> 17:32.887
Now go see to the kids,
and don't bring them out until I say so.

17:45.531 --> 17:50.241
After we confirmed the two deaths
and searched the rest of the premises,

17:52.004 --> 17:54.006
that's when we found the two children.

17:54.340 --> 17:56.286
I mean, we got very lucky.

17:56.609 --> 18:01.080
Uh, we just as easily could've been
chewed to pieces by that AK

18:02.114 --> 18:03.525
on approach.

18:17.430 --> 18:21.606
I can say
that I walked away from the experience

18:23.369 --> 18:27.317
with a greater respect
for the sanctity of human life, you know.

18:28.374 --> 18:29.785
Thank you, Detective.

18:29.875 --> 18:31.718
I believe I speak for the board
when I commend you

18:31.777 --> 18:34.781
on the heroism displayed
by you and Detective Hart.

18:37.083 --> 18:39.324
No, we were doing our jobs, sir.

18:49.395 --> 18:52.740
There were the twig sculptures.

18:54.400 --> 18:58.815
And the LSD on hand
matched that of Dora Lange.

19:01.173 --> 19:05.644
Everybody was pretty satisfied
that we got our man.

19:13.319 --> 19:16.926
The boy had been missing since January.

19:17.490 --> 19:20.096
He'd been dead less than a day.

19:24.163 --> 19:26.769
The girl, she hadn't been reported yet.

19:27.433 --> 19:29.344
She was from Si. Landry.

19:29.802 --> 19:31.543
Catatonic when we found her.

19:38.110 --> 19:40.351
Why should I live in history, huh?

19:41.714 --> 19:44.194
Fuck, I don't wanna know anything anymore.

19:44.817 --> 19:47.627
This is a world where nothing is solved.

19:48.287 --> 19:51.325
Someone once told me
time is a fiat circle,

19:54.660 --> 19:57.641
where everything we've
ever done or will do,

19:57.697 --> 20:00.337
we're gonna do over and
over and over again.

20:01.467 --> 20:05.677
And that little boy and that little girl,
they're gonna be in that room

20:06.672 --> 20:07.844
again.

20:10.242 --> 20:11.812
And again.

20:12.745 --> 20:13.985
And again.

20:15.981 --> 20:16.982
Forever.

20:17.817 --> 20:20.229
Cohle. Couldn't manage to get shot?

20:20.319 --> 20:21.320
Next time.

20:22.488 --> 20:24.525
- Thanks for not doubting us.
- Never did.

20:24.590 --> 20:28.003
Here they come. Marty, our hero!

20:29.328 --> 20:30.932
Way to go, boys.

20:33.666 --> 20:35.771
Little extra pouring

20:36.736 --> 20:38.340
while I finish this up

20:39.004 --> 20:41.177
with the semi-celebrities?

20:41.407 --> 20:45.514
There's plenty of news stories,
if you care to find them.

20:45.578 --> 20:49.458
I got promoted to Detective Sergeant.

20:49.548 --> 20:54.258
Rust got a commendation for bravery,
basically because I insisted.

20:54.854 --> 20:57.130
And things were

20:58.858 --> 21:01.464
pretty good for a while, I guess.

21:03.362 --> 21:04.864
Come on, get your speed up.

21:07.967 --> 21:10.709
Ooh. All right.

21:20.713 --> 21:22.317
Maggie came around.

21:23.048 --> 21:26.791
Just, you know, a lot
of talking, counseling.

21:26.886 --> 21:29.628
And maybe being in a shootout

21:29.722 --> 21:32.601
kind of opened her up to forgiveness,

21:34.727 --> 21:36.468
or the possibility.

21:36.962 --> 21:38.908
Right to the wall. Right lo the wall.

21:39.231 --> 21:41.074
- Yeah. Yeah.
- Oh!

21:41.267 --> 21:43.679
Oh, thank God.

21:44.236 --> 21:46.113
All right. Go take off your skates.
It's time to go.

21:46.172 --> 21:48.743
- One more time, one more time.
- No. No. Please, please, one more time.

21:48.808 --> 21:50.981
All right. One more time around,
then take them off, okay?

21:51.076 --> 21:52.817
Is Daddy coming home yet?

21:52.912 --> 21:53.913
One more time around.

21:53.979 --> 21:55.754
Go on, One more time. One more time.

21:55.815 --> 21:57.021
Okay.

21:59.752 --> 22:01.356
Thanks. I needed that.

22:02.254 --> 22:03.699
I think they did, too.

22:05.758 --> 22:08.102
- Were there others?
- What?

22:09.261 --> 22:11.207
Besides her, were there others?

22:14.033 --> 22:15.034
No.

22:16.702 --> 22:17.703
No.

22:18.771 --> 22:22.048
Maggie, listen, that was
a different person.

22:23.108 --> 22:26.612
I lost it, you know, just a little.

22:28.714 --> 22:31.126
I'm back. I'm begging.

22:32.284 --> 22:35.288
I'll keep begging.
I'll go to my grave begging you.

22:36.722 --> 22:38.827
It's not just the affair.

22:41.460 --> 22:43.064
You used to be a good man.

22:46.298 --> 22:50.804
I've cut the booze, five weeks now.
I'm in a program, Promise Keepers.

23:01.914 --> 23:03.916
You have a long road to climb.

23:05.718 --> 23:06.992
Yes, I do.

23:16.896 --> 23:18.341
Few years,

23:19.598 --> 23:20.872
good ones.

23:24.270 --> 23:27.843
Down the line, one of those
set-ups Maggie was so intent on

23:27.907 --> 23:29.181
finally m.

23:29.241 --> 23:30.686
Doctor, no less.

23:31.010 --> 23:34.014
Yeah, she and Rust had a thing, few years.

23:36.215 --> 23:37.751
He's conﬂict-oriented,

23:37.850 --> 23:41.525
so, when I deny him small arguments,
it builds up his energy.

23:43.188 --> 23:44.292
- Wow.
- Wow.

23:44.390 --> 23:45.926
Yeah!

23:46.025 --> 23:48.528
Are you ever a match for this dude!

23:51.030 --> 23:52.976
Look, you know about Rust.

23:53.065 --> 23:54.442
During those seven years,

23:54.533 --> 23:58.140
he probably pulled more assists
than any other detective in the state.

23:58.237 --> 24:00.148
Word got around quick.

24:00.239 --> 24:04.119
You want a confession,
see if State Detective Cohle's available.

24:05.244 --> 24:06.814
Your interview technique,

24:06.912 --> 24:09.722
I'm sure there's some
secret you can pass on.

24:16.989 --> 24:20.436
Look, everybody knows
there's something wrong with them.

24:21.260 --> 24:23.001
They just don't know what it is.

24:24.063 --> 24:25.974
Everybody wants a confession.

24:26.065 --> 24:30.241
Everybody wants some cathartic narrative
for it. The guilty, especially.

24:32.104 --> 24:33.947
Oh, but everybody's guilty.

24:49.154 --> 24:51.930
You know the good years
when you're in them.

24:51.991 --> 24:55.165
Or you just wait for them
until you get ass cancer

24:56.161 --> 24:59.540
and realize that the good years
came and went.

25:01.100 --> 25:04.775
'Cause there's a feeling...
You might notice it sometimes.

25:04.837 --> 25:07.215
This feeling like life has

25:08.440 --> 25:10.613
slipped through your fingers.

25:15.114 --> 25:17.116
Like the future's behind you.

25:18.617 --> 25:20.290
Like it's always been behind you.

25:23.288 --> 25:27.464
You know, I cleaned up,
but maybe I didn't change.

25:28.560 --> 25:30.233
Not the way I needed to.

25:30.329 --> 25:31.672
Give I! back.

25:35.634 --> 25:37.045
Give it back!

25:37.136 --> 25:40.310
Remember what I said
about the detectives curse?

25:40.906 --> 25:44.479
The solution to my whole life
was right under my nose.

25:45.577 --> 25:48.148
That woman, those kids...

25:52.518 --> 25:55.021
And I was watching everything else.

26:02.561 --> 26:05.337
See, infidelity is one kind of sin.

26:05.664 --> 26:09.407
But my true failure was inattention.

26:11.103 --> 26:12.605
I understand that now.

26:48.907 --> 26:50.215
Hey, Audrey!

26:55.147 --> 26:57.491
So when do you think
things started to,

26:58.050 --> 27:01.998
how you put it, change again,
with Detective Cohle?

27:04.490 --> 27:06.163
Early on' 2002.

27:06.892 --> 27:11.068
But that was his life.
Mine was steady, like I said.

27:12.064 --> 27:15.807
I'm just trying to understand.
What is it you're going for?

27:15.901 --> 27:18.074
What's the, uh, message?

27:19.404 --> 27:21.816
There is no message. lt's just me.

27:21.907 --> 27:25.912
What's just you? Your hair? Your clothes?

27:27.079 --> 27:29.423
I mean, I look at Macie...

27:29.481 --> 27:32.189
Women don't have to look
like you want them to, Dad.

27:32.284 --> 27:35.322
No, women.
But I'm talking about my teenage daughter.

27:35.420 --> 27:37.491
And I'm not trying to tell you
what to wear or anything.

27:37.589 --> 27:39.000
I'm just trying to understand it.

27:39.091 --> 27:41.332
Well, who told you you had to understand?

27:41.426 --> 27:42.427
Why would you?

27:53.672 --> 27:54.673
So,

27:55.674 --> 27:57.051
I hear you made cheerleader.

27:57.276 --> 27:59.984
Yeah, there were like 10 other girls
who didn't get it.

28:00.512 --> 28:01.513
Hmm...

28:01.880 --> 28:03.800
I didn't know they had
eighth-grade cheerleaders.

28:04.049 --> 28:06.893
- Well...
- Same as there's football players.

28:27.839 --> 28:29.876
Tell us
what you know about his girl.

28:30.175 --> 28:31.813
Yeah, uh, Laurie.

28:32.477 --> 28:37.324
Yeah. She became chief of something.
Lafayette General, I believe.

28:37.382 --> 28:39.328
You know what happened there
between them?

28:40.819 --> 28:43.561
What always happens
between men and women.

28:43.655 --> 28:44.861
Reality.

29:08.680 --> 29:11.024
- Dad...
- Tell it to your mother.

29:27.032 --> 29:28.978
Deputy found her

29:29.868 --> 29:31.745
parked in a car with two boys.

29:31.803 --> 29:33.874
Come here. Get over here.

29:39.544 --> 29:40.750
What?

29:42.881 --> 29:46.385
Yeah, in states of undress. You know...

29:47.953 --> 29:49.296
Like fucking.

29:50.255 --> 29:51.928
Boys are 19 and 20.

29:52.391 --> 29:54.132
Got them in holding for the night.

29:54.226 --> 29:57.435
Haven't decided
whether to press statch rape charges.

29:57.496 --> 29:59.100
- What?
- You can't do that.

29:59.164 --> 30:01.804
I can do anything
I goddamn want to those boys.

30:01.900 --> 30:03.174
You think about that.

30:03.268 --> 30:05.771
Audrey. Look at me.

30:07.572 --> 30:09.108
Look at me!

30:09.574 --> 30:12.418
What are you thinking? God!

30:13.812 --> 30:17.419
What the fuck is wrong with you? Huh?

30:17.683 --> 30:20.926
Or is this one of those things
that I'll never understand?

30:21.086 --> 30:25.159
You know, being the captain
of the varsity slut team.

30:25.357 --> 30:26.358
Marty!

30:28.026 --> 30:29.369
Fuck you.

30:38.770 --> 30:41.114
- Get in your fucking room!
- Ow!

30:47.112 --> 30:50.116
- Mom, she hit my head.
- Go to bed. This isn't about you.

30:52.884 --> 30:54.227
Audrey, open the door.

30:55.954 --> 30:57.797
Open the door, Audrey.

31:02.894 --> 31:04.805
Audrey, it's just you and me, honey.

31:06.965 --> 31:08.069
See...

31:10.635 --> 31:12.478
You need to tell me what's going on.

31:14.072 --> 31:16.712
Audrey' open the door, please.

31:20.212 --> 31:21.316
Years.

31:22.047 --> 31:25.392
You ever heard of something called
the M-brane theory, Detectives?

31:25.650 --> 31:28.324
No, that's... That's over my head.

31:28.553 --> 31:31.159
It's like, in this universe,

31:32.157 --> 31:35.502
we process time linearly.

31:36.161 --> 31:37.162
Forward.

31:39.998 --> 31:42.604
But outside of our space-time,

31:43.502 --> 31:46.779
from what would be
a fourth-dimensional perspective,

31:47.339 --> 31:49.216
time wouldn't exist.

31:51.343 --> 31:54.552
And from that vantage, could we attain it,

31:57.215 --> 31:58.455
we'd see

32:02.287 --> 32:04.426
our space-time would look flattened.

32:05.390 --> 32:08.234
Like a single sculpture of matter

32:08.293 --> 32:11.638
in a superposition
of every place it ever occupied.

32:13.565 --> 32:17.707
Our sentience
just cycling through our lives like

32:18.804 --> 32:20.545
carts on a track.

32:26.878 --> 32:29.984
See, everything outside our dimension,

32:31.750 --> 32:33.058
that's eternity.

32:33.919 --> 32:36.832
Eternity looking down on us.

32:38.890 --> 32:40.665
Now, to us,

32:42.227 --> 32:43.467
it's a sphere.

32:44.763 --> 32:46.174
But to them,

32:49.067 --> 32:50.478
it's a circle.

32:58.009 --> 32:59.488
Mr. Cohle.

33:06.418 --> 33:07.453
Mr. Cohle.

33:08.753 --> 33:10.926
What happened in 2002?

33:14.626 --> 33:17.106
Guy Leonard Francis.

33:18.363 --> 33:21.037
They say you killed two
people in Livingston.

33:23.101 --> 33:26.173
They say you're the drug store robber.

33:27.272 --> 33:30.048
You know they already
got a nickname for you?

33:31.309 --> 33:35.724
Southern Fried Pharmacy Firearm Thief.

33:37.349 --> 33:39.522
You like that? Got a nice ring to it.

33:39.618 --> 33:41.393
Bit of a mouthful. Fuck.

33:42.687 --> 33:44.496
I'm telling you, man,
the shit they got these days,

33:44.556 --> 33:47.560
technology, fingerprints, DNA.

33:47.692 --> 33:50.036
You gotta be a fucking genius
to get past that shit.

33:50.128 --> 33:52.665
Let's face it, Francis,
you ain't no fucking genius, are you?

33:54.165 --> 33:57.806
First you come in and say,
"I got the drugs from somewhere else."

33:58.136 --> 34:01.811
Then you say, "No, I don't remember.
I don't remember where I got the drugs."

34:02.474 --> 34:04.317
You're making it too complicated.

34:04.376 --> 34:07.296
You're creating a maze for yourself
that you ain't never gonna get out of.

34:07.345 --> 34:08.824
They got you.

34:09.180 --> 34:10.989
You just gotta change your play.

34:12.717 --> 34:14.253
You gotta plead impairment.

34:14.986 --> 34:16.363
You know what that means?

34:17.822 --> 34:20.325
That means
that you cannot be held accountable

34:21.192 --> 34:22.671
for your actions.

34:23.261 --> 34:26.105
Well, I don't think I ought lo be blamed,

34:26.531 --> 34:29.876
entirely blamed for things I did

34:29.935 --> 34:32.745
when I was under the influence of anything.

34:33.238 --> 34:34.945
I don't think you should either.

34:35.907 --> 34:38.183
That's what I'm saying. PCP.

34:39.210 --> 34:41.190
Stuff makes a man crazy.

34:41.580 --> 34:43.560
One time, a famous case,

34:44.449 --> 34:47.259
a guy, he cut off his
own face on that shit.

34:47.352 --> 34:48.352
- For real?
- Yeah.

34:48.386 --> 34:51.959
You mix that with meth, that's an
insanity defense if I ever heard one.

34:52.190 --> 34:54.864
How are you gonna say
a man who's not on anything

34:54.926 --> 34:56.928
is insane 'cause he did something crazy,

34:57.028 --> 34:59.907
but a man who's on something
that made him crazy

34:59.965 --> 35:01.706
is sane, you know what I mean?

35:01.766 --> 35:03.609
- Works both ways.
- Yeah, exactly.

35:03.702 --> 35:05.782
I mean, I'm not even saying
that I remember anything.

35:05.870 --> 35:07.110
I was shit hammered.

35:07.205 --> 35:09.378
Here we go. That's your play. Right there.

35:09.541 --> 35:11.714
Fuck this amnesia story.

35:12.377 --> 35:13.754
That dirt don't stick.

35:15.213 --> 35:17.124
But insanity defense,

35:18.817 --> 35:20.091
that's your ticket.

35:21.052 --> 35:22.326
That's your way out.

35:23.221 --> 35:26.725
Right? 'Cause you sobered up now.
You got your mind right.

35:27.826 --> 35:29.066
You're back.

35:30.228 --> 35:31.935
You gotta show them the difference

35:32.163 --> 35:36.475
between that madman in that pharmacy
who blew them two people away,

35:36.568 --> 35:38.741
and the man who's sitting here right now.

35:40.505 --> 35:41.916
You gotta show shock.

35:42.774 --> 35:45.084
Terror and re-fucking-morse.

35:45.243 --> 35:47.484
I am. l do. I'm...

35:48.747 --> 35:50.090
I'm scared, sir.

35:50.148 --> 35:52.594
Yeah, you should be. Right?

35:53.151 --> 35:55.324
Now, what'd you say to the pharmacist?

35:58.757 --> 36:01.431
I said, "Give me everything."

36:01.760 --> 36:03.137
And then what?

36:03.862 --> 36:07.105
Boom! Boom!
Blew that fucker away, didn't you?

36:10.368 --> 36:12.279
You want forgiveness for that?

36:13.638 --> 36:15.515
- Yeah.
- Say it.

36:16.608 --> 36:18.519
- I want it.
- You want what?

36:19.678 --> 36:21.123
Forgiveness.

36:26.384 --> 36:28.159
You see what you just did?

36:31.022 --> 36:33.229
You just copped to a double murder.

36:36.327 --> 36:37.965
They got you now.

36:45.136 --> 36:46.809
I wanna make a deal.

36:48.306 --> 36:49.717
A deal about what?

36:50.975 --> 36:52.477
I know things.

36:52.977 --> 36:55.753
What do you know now, all of a sudden?

36:57.916 --> 36:59.190
I know...

37:00.351 --> 37:02.092
I know who you are.

37:03.088 --> 37:06.331
And I know about that woman
y'all found out in the woods, way back.

37:08.560 --> 37:10.039
- The antlers.
- Hmm.

37:13.231 --> 37:15.734
That don't mean shit.
That was in the newspaper.

37:16.601 --> 37:18.012
What do you know'?

37:18.603 --> 37:20.514
You don't know shit, do you?

37:20.572 --> 37:21.573
No.

37:22.340 --> 37:24.411
Y'all never caught the man who did that.

37:25.410 --> 37:26.787
He's been out there,

37:27.712 --> 37:28.782
killing.

37:29.047 --> 37:31.027
You talking out your ass, boy.

37:32.517 --> 37:36.590
You don't know a fucking thing. You're
just trying to buy some time, ain't you?

37:36.688 --> 37:38.065
I met him once.

37:40.058 --> 37:43.039
There's big people who know about him.

37:43.762 --> 37:44.866
Big People.

37:44.929 --> 37:47.239
Ain't no deal, 'cause
there ain't no people.

37:47.298 --> 37:50.108
You make me a deal.
You deal with me about these murders.

37:50.201 --> 37:52.909
Ain't no deal. You ain't got nothing,
because you're full of shit.

37:52.971 --> 37:55.713
And there ain't nobody alive
that did none of that killing.

37:56.241 --> 37:57.549
He's dead, boy.

38:00.211 --> 38:01.417
Ru tell you

38:01.813 --> 38:03.724
about the Yellow King.

38:09.621 --> 38:12.124
What the fuck did you say, boy?

38:12.223 --> 38:13.463
Give me a name.

38:15.894 --> 38:17.635
Give me a fucking name.

38:17.929 --> 38:19.738
Fucking say it, boy.

38:19.831 --> 38:21.333
The Yellow King!

38:22.834 --> 38:24.814
Get off me! Get the hell off me!

38:24.903 --> 38:26.405
No, don't! Get off him!

38:26.471 --> 38:28.109
Make a deal with me!

38:28.239 --> 38:30.913
Deal with me, you son of a bitch!

38:30.975 --> 38:32.318
You deal with me!

38:32.410 --> 38:34.356
Get out of here!

38:34.612 --> 38:37.422
Easy! Calm down, man. Calm down.

38:38.082 --> 38:39.686
Take a deep breath, all right?

38:40.251 --> 38:42.492
You got the confession,
then you made it inadmissible.

38:42.587 --> 38:43.827
What do you fucking mean?
He's still talking.

38:43.922 --> 38:46.129
He's shucking and jiving.
He knows exactly who you are.

38:46.191 --> 38:47.499
You called me in here, huh? You did.

38:47.592 --> 38:49.503
I know. And if we need anything else,
we'll let you know.

38:49.594 --> 38:50.937
We appreciate the assist, Detective.

38:50.995 --> 38:52.668
What the fuck is going on here?

38:52.764 --> 38:55.324
We have to salvage a double murder
confession is what's going on.

38:56.801 --> 38:59.941
If he wasn't just running you in there,
you'll get anything we get.

39:00.605 --> 39:01.675
You have my word.

39:02.006 --> 39:03.508
Come on. Ease up, baby. Calm down.

39:03.608 --> 39:05.110
- I'll be back. Hear me?
- I got it.

39:05.276 --> 39:06.516
Tomorrow.

39:07.212 --> 39:08.657
Stay the fuck back, I got it.

39:34.205 --> 39:37.652
In eternity, where there is no time,

39:39.244 --> 39:42.384
nothing can grow, nothing can become.

39:44.148 --> 39:45.991
Nothing changes.

39:48.653 --> 39:51.099
So, death created time

39:51.723 --> 39:54.670
to grow the things that it would kill.

39:56.661 --> 39:58.402
And you are reborn.

39:59.831 --> 40:01.833
But into the same life

40:03.201 --> 40:05.272
that you've always been born into.

40:06.437 --> 40:10.078
And how many times
have we had this conversation, Detectives?

40:11.442 --> 40:12.853
Well, who knows?

40:15.580 --> 40:18.390
When you can't remember your lives,

40:19.617 --> 40:22.359
you can't change your lives.

40:24.722 --> 40:28.534
And that is the terrible
and secret fate of all life.

40:31.863 --> 40:33.467
You're trapped

40:36.534 --> 40:40.243
by that nightmare you keep waking up into.

40:46.044 --> 40:47.284
You all right?

40:49.714 --> 40:51.421
We gotta go to Abbeville.

40:53.451 --> 40:55.431
We got a deposition this afternoon.

40:55.486 --> 40:57.898
Push it. I got somebody we need to talk to.

40:57.956 --> 41:00.266
I'll tell you on the way. Come on.

41:03.895 --> 41:06.899
You really think he's serious
about having something?

41:07.432 --> 41:08.809
And if so, then what?

41:13.905 --> 41:18.149
Reggie Ledoux deserved to die' Marty.
That was justice.

41:19.911 --> 41:22.084
But I'm not ruling out other agencies.

41:23.314 --> 41:25.260
Mmm-hmm. What does that mean?

41:27.085 --> 41:30.294
Guy Francis and Charlie Lange
both say the Yellow King.

41:31.756 --> 41:34.703
Dora Lange said the Yellow King.

41:39.263 --> 41:44.110
Okay, look, if the killer's still out
there, why haven! there been more killings?

41:44.602 --> 41:47.776
Well' maybe there have, Many,
and we just don't know about them.

41:47.839 --> 41:49.546
Haven't put them together.

41:52.944 --> 41:56.289
Ever wonder why that task force
was so hot to take the case

41:56.781 --> 41:58.021
back in '95?

41:59.817 --> 42:02.821
Are you telling me
you think the task force was in on it?

42:18.169 --> 42:19.375
Fuck!

42:26.844 --> 42:28.585
How the fuck does this happen?

42:28.679 --> 42:30.522
You know what he was looking at
with the double murders.

42:30.581 --> 42:32.652
Guess he thought about
it and made a choice.

42:34.552 --> 42:35.690
You got a camera feed?

42:41.492 --> 42:43.369
Here, go back. Play this.

42:45.696 --> 42:48.609
He took a phone call
at 7:15. His lawyer.

43:10.755 --> 43:12.860
You got audio on this? Sound?

43:12.924 --> 43:14.267
No, just the vid.

43:19.697 --> 43:21.904
That's it. Just
three hours of nothing.

43:24.535 --> 43:26.208
Till you see the blood.

43:37.248 --> 43:40.286
We don't know what somebody
might have told him on that phone call.

43:40.384 --> 43:42.455
I wanna see your incoming call logs now.

43:43.488 --> 43:44.728
All right.

43:45.556 --> 43:47.467
What are the two officers' names?

43:47.558 --> 43:49.231
Childress and Mahoney.

43:49.293 --> 43:51.637
- Give me their files, please.
- Yes, sir.

44:18.823 --> 44:21.429
- Terrence, get prints on this.
- Yes, sir.

44:21.492 --> 44:22.527
Prints?

44:22.760 --> 44:24.296
That's a public phone.

44:25.163 --> 44:27.370
No kind of lawyer makes calls from here.

44:29.467 --> 44:32.971
- Francis have relatives?
- Yeah, sisters. A few nieces, nephews.

44:34.138 --> 44:36.675
Connects to the suicide how'?

44:36.874 --> 44:38.876
Well, somebody might have
told him something.

44:40.011 --> 44:41.649
Gave him no choice.

44:46.117 --> 44:47.494
Well, great.

44:48.119 --> 44:50.159
So, when he got
going on this thing again,

44:50.221 --> 44:51.996
did he mention Billy Lee Tuttle?

44:52.323 --> 44:53.893
You know that he did.

44:53.991 --> 44:57.131
Turtle died a couple of years back. 2010.

44:57.795 --> 45:02.471
Yeah. Yeah, what was that?
Uh, mixed medications? So what?

45:02.533 --> 45:05.013
Right after Cohle showed
back up in the state.

45:08.139 --> 45:09.641
Fuck this.

45:10.641 --> 45:11.711
Fuck this bullshit.

45:11.809 --> 45:14.915
You tell me right now
why you're all over Cohle,

45:15.479 --> 45:16.924
or I'll walk.

46:38.729 --> 46:41.073
His record. His reports, his stories.

46:41.399 --> 46:42.469
They don't add up.

46:42.566 --> 46:45.775
So talk to him about it already.
Stop pissing in my ear.

46:45.836 --> 46:48.112
- We did.
- Oh, you did?

46:49.607 --> 46:50.642
What?

46:51.609 --> 46:54.249
Well, if you two talked to Rust

46:54.779 --> 46:56.656
and you weren't getting a read on him,

46:57.748 --> 46:59.921
he was getting a read on you.

47:37.154 --> 47:39.065
This is all you got?

47:40.458 --> 47:42.301
Fuck, I already know all this.

47:43.461 --> 47:45.532
And what we have, so far.

47:45.696 --> 47:47.471
You hadn't checked old unsolveds.

47:47.631 --> 47:49.542
Maybe you stop dancing with us.

47:50.634 --> 47:52.705
Tell us what you've really been up to.

47:53.471 --> 47:54.916
How you spend your time.

47:55.172 --> 47:57.482
I already told you how I spend my time.

47:57.541 --> 47:59.578
Except you've been bullshitting us
all afternoon.

47:59.677 --> 48:01.679
Excuse us for one minute, please.

49:14.285 --> 49:16.765
These are from the crime scene
in Lake Charles.

49:16.821 --> 49:18.391
Once folks got word.

49:23.961 --> 49:25.599
Recognize anybody in there?

49:27.765 --> 49:30.336
Lake Charles is a bit
out of the way for you, ain't it?

49:30.434 --> 49:32.505
How'd you
keep her out of the papers?

49:33.003 --> 49:34.744
Maybe you got some friends in

49:36.106 --> 49:37.346
high places?

49:38.242 --> 49:41.280
Your truck
and a man fitting your description

49:41.345 --> 49:44.087
was spotted in the vicinity
of our crime scene

49:44.148 --> 49:47.857
five times, by five different people
over the last month.

49:56.927 --> 50:00.602
Now, besides people seeing him and
his truck around the location for weeks,

50:00.664 --> 50:02.974
you know he was off the grid
after he left in '02.

50:03.200 --> 50:06.204
Didn't show up anywhere till 2010.
Louisiana.

50:07.771 --> 50:10.183
Got his driver's license renewed.

50:11.675 --> 50:14.884
Nobody knows what he's been doing
in the meantime.

50:15.312 --> 50:17.314
He's got a storage shed
near Church Point.

50:17.715 --> 50:19.456
He won't let us see what's inside.

50:39.570 --> 50:41.846
How about you let us see
what you're keeping in storage?

50:41.972 --> 50:44.714
Fuck no, you can't see my storage unit.

50:45.709 --> 50:46.744
Get a warrant.

50:47.144 --> 50:49.385
Christ, try working a case.

50:49.480 --> 50:50.982
- We are working it.
- Yeah?

50:51.048 --> 50:55.827
See, how we work it is, we think way back.
You put the case on Rianne Olivier.

50:55.886 --> 50:57.661
Put it on her old boyfriend.

50:58.322 --> 51:00.666
I don't know,
maybe the Ledoux boys knew you.

51:01.058 --> 51:03.436
Maybe you traveled the same circles.

51:03.527 --> 51:05.268
Got the same hobbies.

51:05.863 --> 51:07.672
Maybe they had something on you.

51:07.731 --> 51:09.811
You just kept pulling
the right old murders,

51:09.833 --> 51:12.040
take the case wherever you wanted it to go.

51:12.670 --> 51:13.842
You're a juicer.

51:14.438 --> 51:15.439
Ever black out?

51:15.539 --> 51:17.541
Ever wake up,
don't remember what happened?

51:26.183 --> 51:29.221
Look, y'all want to arrest me, go ahead.

51:31.055 --> 51:32.534
You want to follow me...

51:34.024 --> 51:36.561
Come on. You want to see something?

51:39.530 --> 51:40.941
Get a warrant.

51:44.134 --> 51:45.477
Thanks for the beer.

51:46.303 --> 51:50.080
Beyond that,
you wasted my fucking day, company men.

52:36.520 --> 52:38.693
Now, he bartends
four days a week.

52:38.789 --> 52:40.791
This roadhouse
has a little apartment behind it.

52:40.858 --> 52:42.860
No other accounting of his time.

52:42.960 --> 52:44.303
Says he drinks.

52:45.796 --> 52:47.207
You're wrong.

52:47.998 --> 52:51.002
Nobody could change that much.
You are dead wrong.

52:51.101 --> 52:54.014
Hey, you've been telling us all day
about the kind of shit he'd think up.

52:54.104 --> 52:56.607
Way he'd talk.
We got a good earful of that, too.

52:56.674 --> 52:59.280
You're gonna tell me
that's a stable individual?

52:59.343 --> 53:01.687
Left a burnout, junkie rumors.

53:01.779 --> 53:04.350
You think 10 years on the sauce
has made him more reasonable?

53:05.382 --> 53:09.125
Think about this. You said it.
He'd been there three months.

53:09.319 --> 53:12.459
And you two catch a heater
like you've never had before or since.

53:12.523 --> 53:14.867
One that he shines on.

53:15.025 --> 53:17.198
You saying he did such a great job.

53:18.295 --> 53:20.297
Didn't he get you every bit of evidence?

53:20.464 --> 53:22.705
Didn't he push you where
he wanted it to go?

53:23.300 --> 53:26.975
He brought you Rianne Olivier.
She wasn't one of Ledoux's.

53:27.971 --> 53:29.382
She was one of his.

53:29.840 --> 53:31.877
What'd he say? "Life is a disease"?

53:32.142 --> 53:35.555
When he heard the Abbeville prisoner,
Francis, knew something, he got on it.

53:35.646 --> 53:36.716
He shut it down.

53:36.814 --> 53:39.214
You ever thought if he made that
phone call to the prisoner'?

53:39.216 --> 53:41.924
Like, I don't know,
the guy was trying to blackmail him?

53:42.019 --> 53:44.090
He got on that, too, didn't he?

53:44.354 --> 53:46.425
The idea that the Lange killer
was still out there.

53:49.526 --> 53:50.732
Yeah.

53:50.828 --> 53:52.830
Yeah. Yeah, he did.

53:53.530 --> 53:55.339
Looking for a new patsy, maybe.

54:39.643 --> 54:41.645
Y'all are giving me a lotto absorb.

54:41.979 --> 54:44.220
You're goddamn right
it's a lot to absorb.

54:44.548 --> 54:46.425
- So help us out.
- Yeah.

54:47.251 --> 54:51.495
Whatever you can tell us about, you know,
from when he got on the Lange killer,

54:51.588 --> 54:54.000
up to when you two had your altercation.

54:54.091 --> 54:55.934
Whatever that was about.
